muse-alab runs Meta's Muse Code command-line program (`muse`) as a separate process. It
does not include, modify or redistribute any part of that program; `muse` is installed and
licensed separately, by its vendor's terms, through aterm's package manager. Muse Code is a
name of its vendor.

Parts of muse-alab follow aterm's source (Apache-2.0, the same author): the package store
layout and build numbering of its package manager (crates/atpkg), and Muse Code's resume
grammar, exit table, session witness and quiet-restart gates from its harness lanes
(crates/aterm-agent/src/harness/upgrade_muse*.rs). The file and function each comes from
is cited where it is used.
